GradingAssignments (40%); Mid term presentations (30%); End term exam (30%)Notebook Review Report AssignmentsChoose and explore at least 10 interactive notebooks from the course website. Submit a handwritten report with one clearly labelled entry for each chosen notebook.For each notebook, your entry should include:The notebook title and the widget you explored.A concise explanation of the scientific demonstration: what physical concept the widget illustrates, which controls you changed, and what you observed.Two concrete suggestions to improve the widget. Each suggestion should explain why it would improve the scientific demonstration, clarity, usability, or interpretation.One possible physics bug, limitation, or questionable assumption. Explain the reasoning behind your concern; you do not need to prove that it is an error.Marks will be awarded primarily for the quality of the two suggested improvements: their logic, relevance to the notebook, and connection to the science being demonstrated. Additional bonus marks will be awarded for identifying a plausible physics bug or limitation and supporting it with sound reasoning.Mid/End Term ExamsOpen book exams, where you will have access to textbook chapters/ other reading material. The exam duration will be 3 Hrs.
The only thing that will not be allowed is interaction with peers.

